          "title": "Brandeln",
          "subtitle": "Trick-taking",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Brandeln is a historical German Nap-like trick-taking game in which the bidder plays alone against the other players."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "A historical German game also called Brandle, described as a Nap equivalent with solo bidding."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "3-4 players use the table arrangement described for Brandeln."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "28-card French or German pack"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "28-card French or German pack, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal from a 28-card pack, then allow players to bid for the right to name the contract or trump."
            }
